# firmware/main/Kconfig.projbuild
menu "Clawd Configuration"
    config CLAWD_WIFI_ENABLED
        bool "Enable WiFi (debug/setup)"
        default n
        help
            Enable WiFi for OTA updates and debug logging.
            Not needed for normal BLE notification operation.

    config CLAWD_LCD_TURN_180
        bool "MiniBar bar: turn the picture 180 degrees"
        default n
        help
            The bar's AXS15231B panel is 172 x 640 portrait, drawn as 640 x 172 by software rotation in display.c.
            Upright (side buttons on top) is LVGL rotation 270 on the Waveshare ESP32-S3-Touch-LCD-3.49 V2, as the
            MiniBar project found on the board; turn this on (rotation 90) if the picture comes up upside down.

    config CLAWD_SLEEP_BRIGHTNESS
        int "MiniBar bar: backlight level while Clawd sleeps (0 to 255)"
        range 0 255
        default 20
        help
            When the daemon reports no active Claude session, the firmware shows Clawd asleep. Upstream turns the
            backlight off then (0 here), which leaves a desk bar black. The default dims it so the sleeping Clawd stays
            visible. The level is never brighter than the brightness set over BLE (default 102).
endmenu
